1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:03,825
Here's a manager's quick walkthrough: follow up on a repair,

2
00:00:03,825 --> 00:00:07,898
correct a cash charge, and check how the rooms are performing.

3
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:17,131
On Rooms, open Maintenance. Select the room and describe the
problem. Here, room one oh one has a loose bathroom tap.

4
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:25,117
Once the tap is repaired, select Mark fixed. Filter to Fixed to
find the issue and see when it was resolved.

5
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:32,122
For a cash correction, search Reservations for the guest's
booking. Here, we're looking for Maya Mensah.

6
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:40,189
Open the folio and select View receipt on the original payment.
Check what Maya paid before you return cash.

7
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:45,304
Open your own cash shift before processing the refund. Enter the

8
00:00:45,304 --> 00:00:49,978
opening float so the till reconciliation starts with the correct
amount.

9
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:55,212
Back at the original receipt, enter twenty-five cedis and a
reason,

10
00:00:55,212 --> 00:00:59,995
then record the cash refund. The app displays a refund receipt.

11
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:08,619
On Cash desk, use Counted and Expected to review a closed shift.
Variance shows the difference between those amounts.

12
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:15,748
Close your own shift with the actual cash count. The refund is
included in what the system expects.

13
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:21,575
In Reports, pick a start date and the first date to leave out.
Then run the report.

14
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:28,749
Use room nights and occupancy to see demand. Compare room
revenue, average daily

15
00:01:28,749 --> 00:01:34,468
rate, and revenue per available room to understand the value of
those bookings.
